{"item_id":"feed:/resources/materials/physical-vapor-deposition/","version_id":"fcf9079ad45657e09903d78c29d7b8ae301b4348d9c2d777777b5d1e831378a0","decision":"reject","reason":"Although fresh and manufacturing-relevant, this is a general materials-process explainer rather than evidence about frontier AI for 3D modeling, CAD, or intelligent physical systems. Its coating-property figures are presented without an identified experimental check, and it supplies no AI-enabled geometry, verification, or simulation development.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:/resources/materials/recrystallization-of-metals/","version_id":"ded55799bfd57b9e786dbfccb038115b95d469ba2c6a470457c0869c6e17bd6c","decision":"reject","reason":"This fresh metallurgy overview is outside the publication's lead topics: it reports conventional material science rather than an AI capability for CAD, 3D modeling, or robotics. The excerpt also provides no new, checkable development or stated experimental conditions that would connect recrystallization knowledge to model-assisted engineering decisions.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:/resources/supply-chain/oil-refinery/","version_id":"03628944819a5390db2f0c3005cb2bcb336118528a4d5c646d7dfe25c82500ea","decision":"reject","reason":"The item is a fresh but generic refinery-process guide, with no frontier-model, CAD, 3D-asset, simulation, or robotics development. Its operating figures are not tied to a disclosed check relevant to the editorial core test, so it cannot support a decision about intelligent systems in physical space.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","decision":"accept","reason":"This is fresh, directly relevant CAD-industry reporting with citable passages distinguishing demonstrated workflows from beta, Tech Preview, and planned releases. The conference demonstrations support only that Autodesk showed an assistant identifying a substitute part and preparing a change order, plus connected design workflows; they do not independently establish production reliability, and the article explicitly preserves that availability distinction. As a trade report on one vendor event it is not independent corroboration of Autodesk capability claims, but it is useful commercial perspective alongside the research evidence.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/build-bom-from-wire-harness-drawing","version_id":"1eafb0dcff5f6f5b8c341b6abe613a9a77ce26e7c0fc4eef73af6790f2ae7fe5","decision":"defer","reason":"The workflow is relevant as a CAD-drawing-to-structured-BOM claim, and the passage says estimators review flagged exceptions rather than every line. However, Cableteque is the claimant and the cited KCM result gives no source corpus, extraction accuracy, error categories, review time, attempt count, or independent evaluation; 18 hours to 45 minutes is therefore a vendor-reported case result, not verified performance. A test on revision-controlled customer drawing packages, with line-item recall and compatibility-error results after human review, would make this checkable.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/does-cableteque-quote-extract-boms-automatically-from-customer-pdf-drawings","version_id":"6d917d47e8d4b52b9fe4f0290327adf5dea0f67fa26266abe25051ad74adc0af","decision":"defer","reason":"This is relevant commercial evidence about extracting manufacturing BOMs from PDF drawings, and it usefully specifies that users should compare extracted line items with the source PDF. But the claimed two-minute workflow and up-to-96% savings are Cableteque's own numbers, with no disclosed document set, error rate, attempt count, or independent check. It also repeats the same underlying product claim as the other Cableteque items, so it cannot serve as corroboration; a reproducible evaluation is needed.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/losing-money-on-cable-assembly-quotes","version_id":"33abdbe4f75624efed189d40297ade0c2f12f250f578435d87954b3c34d4693e","decision":"reject","reason":"This is a fresh restatement of Cableteque's drawing-to-BOM, compatibility, pricing, and labor-automation claims rather than a distinct development. Its Resco turnaround result is a vendor-selected customer report without disclosed conditions or independent verification, and the same publisher's related coverage is not corroboration. It adds no checkable evidence beyond the deferred product claims.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/retiring-estimator-quoting-knowledge","version_id":"7684d3f81b48f399e04d30dd15d5c9125d3b3466ed41c07228ed6dc7b4631cc7","decision":"reject","reason":"The practitioner problem—capturing manufacturing-estimator judgment—is relevant, but this item largely restates the same Cableteque automation claims and vendor-reported performance as the other items from the same publisher. The cited survey and Derrick Lang result lack accessible methodology, task conditions, and independent verification in the supplied passage. It therefore does not add novel, checkable evidence for the series.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://cableteque.com/news/ai-wire-harness-quoting-europe","version_id":"3f0b6128cabb2c363faca5fff7b5511c50c36083101892f525858da4428f081b","decision":"defer","reason":"The European expansion is a potentially relevant AI-native startup development, but this is the company's own announcement and it does not independently check that European hosting, distributor integrations, or customer use are operating as described. The passage itself says ISO 27001 certification is only targeted for December 2026, so it cannot support a present-tense security claim. Named customer-access evidence, a demonstrable EU deployment, and confirmed certification status would resolve the uncertainty.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","decision":"accept","reason":"This fresh, highly relevant survey directly addresses editable 3D scenes, parametric CAD, and simulation-to-hardware robotics, while stating what its checks observed: public code, videos, documentation, and benchmark results across 707 cases. Its own limitations are decision-useful: only 132 cases include runnable code, CAD benchmark success does not verify tolerances or manufacturability, and physical controllers were not tested under withheld conditions. It provides a research perspective that complements the commercial Autodesk report, though customer and working-engineer experience remains comparatively absent.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
